{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:dd3d9da4203e4575","name":"Hyperspace Beacon","source":{"id":"source:reference-dd3d9da4203e4575","title":"Hyperspace Beacon","revision":19164,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T21:26:39Z","sha256":"6e931f2777c74386ab4c76313fd4df3406bfb08b38407bcbb1292f54be527fde","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19164","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Hyperspace%20Beacon&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-dd3d9da4203e4575","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["One of the major differences between ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Old Republic Era"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Old_Republic_Era"}," and campaigns set in the classic era is the way hyperspace travel functions. Prior to ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Mandalorian Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Mandalorian_Wars"},", most ",{"tag":"a","children":["Starships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Starships"}," do not have advanced ",{"tag":"a","children":["Navicomputers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Navicomputers"}," built into their ships. Instead, they have simple ",{"tag":"a","children":["Hyperdrive"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hyperdrive","referenceId":"reference:6774bf610b6e6f09"}," operation systems that depended on satellites known as Hyperspace Beacons for navigational data. These beacons record and broadcast navigational data to any ships stopping at that point, keeping them up to date on a small number of routes connected to that beacon. Each Hyperspace Beacon possesses only the smallest amount of computing power, with a basic artificial intelligence built in to keep the beacons from being moved or damaged by stellar anomalies. Hyperspace Beacons are critical to hyperspace travel, as they are the buoys that guide all ships through the space lanes.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["With galactic exploration reaching levels unseen since ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Great Hyperspace War"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Great_Hyperspace_War?action=edit&redlink=1"},", the Republic military invests significant resources in the miniaturization of navigational computers. As a part of the reconstruction efforts during ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Restoration Period"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Restoration_Period"},", the Republic financially sponsors the establishment of a system by which navigational data would be distributed across the galaxy quickly and efficiently, allowing navigators to pull up-to-date hyperspace geography data at any stop. The new ",{"tag":"a","children":["Navicomputers"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Navicomputers"},", coupled with the rapid spread of hyperspace data, reduce the need for Hyperspace Beacons to the point where they are only used on hyperspace routes that have not yet been verified as 100% safe.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["For campaigns set prior to ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Mandalorian Wars"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Mandalorian_Wars"},", or for campaigns set in areas where hyperspace routes have not yet been finalized, Hyperspace Beacons can provide opportunities to challenge the heroes or place them in a dangerous position. If a ship is capable of opening a communications channel to a Hyperspace Beacon, treat that ship as though it has a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Navicomputer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Navicomputer","referenceId":"reference:4ae152610571a224"}," for the purpose of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Astrogation"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Astrogation"},". Otherwise, the ship's navigator will need to make the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Use Computer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Use_Computer","referenceId":"reference:ff8449006aafd27d"}," check without the aid of a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Navicomputer"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Navicomputer","referenceId":"reference:4ae152610571a224"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Default (Untrained)"]},"\n","\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Hyperspace Beacon Statistics (CL 0)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Huge ",{"tag":"a","children":["Space Station"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Space_Station"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," -2; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +0\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 11 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 11), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 21; +3 Armor\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},": 50; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Reduction"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Reduction"},": 5; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Threshold"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Threshold"},": 31\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Offense"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Speed:"]}," Immobile\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Fighting Space"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fighting_Space","referenceId":"reference:cdbf34043baceb78"},":"]}," 3x3 Squares (",{"tag":"a","children":["Charac